WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.020
Mikl: Tell us about...

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.360
Mikl: this was an assignment, I take it?

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.960
Fred: actually, this one, it was early on, and

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:11.560
Fred: I had to I had to keep getting these assignments.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:15.480
Fred: So some unwary magazine said,

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.820
Fred: "Oh yeah go ahead shoot that."

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.640
Fred: I went to the Golden Gate Bridge office and said,

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:27.300
Fred: "I'm a photographer and this magazine wants to do a story on the bridge painters."

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:33.580
Fred: And they said, "Oh yeah, go out and see Joe. 
He's the foreman. He'll fix you up."

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:38.360
Fred: Joe, thought I was really funny.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:44.660
Fred: And I was crawling around the bridge for a couple of weeks. And they were all amused.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:53.920
Fred: And after they saw me running around; a couple times they saved me from doing dangerous things.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:01:02.540
Fred: I must say there were vantage points that I had...

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:08.220
Fred: Photography is all about getting your camera located at the proper viewpoint.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:12.300
Fred: So that's what I was always about .

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:17.600
Fred: That's what made aerials and even underwater necessary.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:24.620
Fred: But here, for instance, I was underneath the roadbed. Which was really the scariest place.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:28.880
Fred: That little thing in the center is Alcatraz.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:37.460
Fred: And when you're beneath the roadbed, there is a very odd sensation. Because you cannot see...

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:41.560
Fred: ...usually cannot see the horizon.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:48.640
Fred: So you look down and, if there's a breeze, you see whitecaps moving underneath you.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:51.960
Fred: And the sensation is that the bridge is falling over.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:58.100
Fred: That is much scarier than being up on top.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:10.900
Fred: Being up on top is achieved by... 
in each tower there is a tiny electric elevator.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:20.600
Fred: And it will accommodate two painters, 
if they hold their lunch bucket on top of their head.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:24.360
Fred: And it goes fairly slowly up to the top.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:31.000
Fred: They've also discovered that you can get
two more guys on top of the cage,

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.940
Fred: if you remember to stop the elevator in time.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:39.100
Fred: Otherwise it's not so good.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.000
Fred: But the first time I got up on top,

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:47.780
Fred: I was so excited that I ran out
and started to run down a cable...

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:54.840
Fred: And one guy said, "Buddy, I think you better come back here. I want to give you a safety belt."

00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:13.419
Fred: And I really appreciated their concern.

